  "answer": "I found no earlier ticket that reports this problem. terminal#1504 is the original request that added the `file.dll,index` icon syntax, and it was closed as fixed. terminal#19813 covers web URLs in `icon`, which were blocked on purpose. Neither one describes indexed icons being rejected by the media-resource validation, or the split on the first comma. Treat this as a new regression. Until it is fixed, you can point `icon` at a standalone .ico or .png file that you extract from the DLL. Your proposed fix is the right one: validate only the binary path, keep the signed index, and split on the last comma in both the validator and `IconPathConverter`. Include the regression tests you listed when you submit it."
 },
